This is for an extremely hideous problem:
```js
function foo(x) {
    bar(x);
}
function bar(x) {
    if (x === 1) {
        throw new Error();
    }
}
foo(3);
foo(2);
foo(1);
```
when `foo` is inlined, it would prevent `bar` from being inlined, but `bar` is alreay `take()`
